{"author": "hattrill", "body": "* **PTHR ID & PTN node:**\n\nPTN000292477\nTRANSMEMBRANE PROTEIN 14, 15 (PTHR12668)\n\n* **Sequences with problematic annotation (ID + gene/protein name):**\ne.g. FB:FBgn0034902 CG5532 IBA 'regulation of heme biosynthetic process\" IBA\ncomes from  mouse Tmem14c https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/Q9CQN6/entry ; MGI:1913404 (IMP)\n\nfrom the [exp source paper ](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25157825/) they suggest that TMEM14C is involved in the transport of protoporphyrinogen IX (CHEBI:57307) across the inner membrane as part of mitochondrial heme biosynthesis and therefore should be annotated as involved_in GO:0006783 heme biosynthetic process rather than regulation of\n\n<img width=\"527\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bd273239-ebd5-42bd-916e-ae6956f8c2ba\" />\n \ntagging @LiNiMGI - could you update the MGI annotation?\n\nand then this should be ok to propagate via PAINT.", "created_at": "2025-02-19T15:32:07Z", "key": "issue", "labels": ["PAINT annotation", "mitochondrion"], "state": "closed", "state_reason": "completed", "title": "PTN000292477 heme biosynthetic process", "type": "issue", "updated_at": "2025-02-20T08:30:34Z"}
